        {
          "_key": "000000000006",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000002",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Kom Ombo, situated in southern "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000004",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000003"
              ],
              "text": "Egypt"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000005",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ", is renowned not just for its ancient temple dedicated to the gods Sobek and Horus, but also for its vibrant food scene that mirrors the confluence of cultures and histories in this region. Dining in Kom Ombo offers a palette of flavours that are both deeply traditional and uniquely reflective of Nubian influences prevalent in Upper Egypt."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000003",
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egypt",
              "newTab": true
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000008",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000007",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Traditional Dishes to Try"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h3"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000000b",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000009",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "strong"
              ],
              "text": "Ta’meya (Egyptian Falafel):"
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000000a",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " Made from fava beans rather than chickpeas, this southern-style falafel is greener, fluffier, and bursting with herbs. Often served for breakfast or as a snack, it’s a fresh and flavourful twist on the regional favourite."
            }
          ],
          "level": 1,
          "listItem": "bullet",
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000000e",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000000c",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "strong"
              ],
              "text": "Ful Medames:"
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000000d",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " A beloved Egyptian staple, ful in Kom Ombo is slow-cooked with garlic, olive oil, and warming spices. Sometimes topped with fresh tomatoes or eggs, it’s a hearty and satisfying way to start the day."
            }
          ],
          "level": 1,
          "listItem": "bullet",
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000011",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000000f",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "strong"
              ],
              "text": "Molokhia:"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000010",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " This rich, leafy green soup is a national favourite. In Kom Ombo, it’s typically served with chicken or rabbit and accompanied by rice or flatbread. Its unique texture and earthy flavour make it a local comfort dish."
            }
          ],
          "level": 1,
          "listItem": "bullet",
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000016",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000012",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "strong"
              ],
              "text": "Grilled Fish and "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000014",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000013"
              ],
              "text": "Nile Seafood: Thanks to Kom Ombo’s"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000015",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " riverside location, fresh fish is abundant. Grilled and seasoned with local herbs, Nile perch and tilapia dishes here are light, healthy, and full of flavour."
            }
          ],
